# Notifier rollout

## Order

No dependency ordering is required. Deploy notifier instances one at a time in the normal release order. Customer can be rolled out independently because `offer.queued {customerId, offerId}` is unchanged; no atomic switch or queue drain is needed.

## Mixed versions

The migration creates `offer_caps` with `IF NOT EXISTS`; existing `sent` rows and queued events are retained. New notifier instances continue consuming the old event shape and count existing `sent` rows for the current platform day, so a restart or a partially completed rollout does not reset the cap. New instances return the additive `capped` field; old clients that read only `count` and `ticks` remain compatible. The drop total is cumulative per customer, while the two-send limit resets at `platform tick / 100`.

## Rollback

Roll back by routing traffic and events back to the previous notifier version. Do not delete or rewrite `sent` or `offer_caps`. The old version ignores the additive table and continues its prior send behavior; after redeployment of the new version, persisted cap/drop data and existing sends are reused. Any queued events remain valid because their payload was not changed.
